ious trials that have been facing  this region for years if not decades and  certainly one that is going to guarantee  to cause a lot of public anger amongst  the pro secessionists me reading what  will the impact be on Catalan on the  Catalan independence movement what what  impact will this verdict have well if  the Spanish government was thinking that  any sort of trial or or jail sentence  imprisonment was going to quell any sort  of feelings of secessionism here well  they might be proved wrong with that  because this is definitely going to  guarantee some kind of reaction from  those Catalan nationalists and those  groups that have been calling out for  that those groups who were in favor of  that illegal referendum as well in fact  they're already calling for peaceful  demonstrations to come out already in  the wake of this sentencing as well  there is going to be a statement from  the Catalan president also a special  extraordinary meeting at the Parliament  as well but already you've had a quite a  strong campaign from the independent  issed to call for people to come out  onto the streets and of course the  Spanish authorities have reacted in kind  as well they've already deployed what is  believed to be up to a thousand riot  police officers in case those those  demonstrations turn violent but of  course the Catalan pro-independence  would say that they've called for  nothing but peaceful demonstrations as  they have always done in the past  Sonia many thanks indeed al Jazeera  Santiago a go there live in Barcelona
 

